  "report_markdown": "# Cap Table \u2014 Cadence\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nModeled 1 scenario(s) for Cadence: 1 full, 0 mixed, 0 repay-only.\n1 counsel-review item(s) surfaced. 14 date-sensitive item(s) in watchlist.\nFounder ownership ranges 63.3% to 63.3% across resolved scenarios.\n\n> \u26a0 **Cap base was NOT produced by the deterministic spreadsheet mapper.** It was entered\n> manually or extracted from a document (PDF / Carta / pasted), so it was not\n> mechanically verified against a structured source. Confirm each holder and class against\n> whatever these figures came from \u2014 the source document if there was one, or your own\n> share records if you described the cap table in conversation \u2014 before relying on them.\n\n## Current Cap State\n\nAs of: 2026-09-30\n\n| Holder | Shares (as-converted) | % of FD |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Alex Stone | 4,000,000 | 44.4% |\n| Sam Lee | 3,500,000 | 38.9% |\n| Options outstanding | 500,000 | 5.6% |\n| Options available | 1,000,000 | 11.1% |\n| **Total fully-diluted** | **9,000,000** | **100.0%** |\n\nOutstanding SAFEs: 1\n\n## Scenarios Modeled\n\n### Series A \u2014 $16M pre / $4M raise (Priced round)\n\n**Stage:** Fully modeled (`full`)\n\n**Inputs:**\n- `pre_money`: 16000000\n- `new_money`: 4000000\n\n**Post-round ownership:**\n- founders pct: 63.3%\n- preferred pct: 0.0%\n- option pool pct: 12.7%\n- safe pct: 4.0%\n- note pct: 0.0%\n- new money pct: 20.0%\n- each founder, post-round:\n  - Alex Stone: 33.8% (4,000,000 shares)\n  - Sam Lee: 29.6% (3,500,000 shares)\n  - *(Founders only. Shares held through employee/other common batches are counted in the totals above but are not broken out per person here.)*\n\n**Equity financing price:** $1.6889/share\n\n**Founder Impact Lens:** Founders collectively held 83.3% of fully-diluted shares before this scenario; after, 63.3%. That's -20.0 percentage points.\n\n**Per-SAFE conversion math:**\n\n| SAFE | Branch | Purchase \u00f7 Cap | Conversion price | Conversion shares |\n|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n| Foobar Capital LLC (`safe_foobar`) | Cap and discount both applied \u2014 whichever gave more shares | \u2014 | $1.0556 | 473,684 |\n\n_Provenance: rules: `safe.post_money_cap_conversion`_\n\n## Counsel Review Required\n\n### Delaware Cross Border\n- **[QSBS rules are date-sensitive](https://www.thetaxadviser.com/issues/2025/dec/revisiting-sec-1202-strategic-planning-after-the-2025-obbba-expansion/)** (`delaware_cross_border.qsbs_date_sensitive`)\n  - US QSBS eligibility and exclusion amounts are date-sensitive and changed for stock issued after July 4, 2025 under OBBBA; cap-table scripts should flag issue date and tax counsel review.\n\n## Date-Sensitive Watchlist\n\n_1 rule(s) to watch (from 1 matched instances)._\n\n| Rule | Status | When | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [QSBS rules are date-sensitive](https://www.thetaxadviser.com/issues/2025/dec/revisiting-sec-1202-strategic-planning-after-the-2025-obbba-expansion/) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the stock issue date for this instance. |\n\n### For-Reference Annotations\n\n_13 item(s) \u2014 rules that don't apply to this engagement in its current state (different jurisdiction, no grants, etc.) but are tracked in case the engagement evolves. No action needed today._\n\n## Sources Cited\n\n- `TAXADVISER-QSBS-OBBBA`\n\n---\n\n## Coaching Commentary\n\n### Your ownership story\n\nWith one scenario modeled \u2014 the Series A at $16M pre-money / $4M raise \u2014 the founders land at **63.3%** post-financing, down from 83.3% pre-round. That is a drop of 20 percentage points in one step.\n\nTwo drivers together explain all 24 percentage points of dilution from the pre-round baseline:\n\n- **New money ($4M in)** accounts for 20pp. This is the straightforward share-issuance cost of the raise itself: new investors receive shares priced at the Series A price, and the founders' slice of the pie shrinks accordingly.\n- **SAFE conversion** accounts for 4pp. The outstanding SAFE converts into equity at this round, adding shares to the denominator before the new money is even counted. The YC post-money SAFE primer (Example 1) explains why: the SAFE investor's shares are priced off the post-money cap, and those shares join the fully-diluted count at closing alongside the new Series A shares.\n\nNo option pool top-up was modeled in this scenario. If the Series A term sheet requires the founders to refresh or increase the option pool before the round closes \u2014 which is common practice \u2014 that top-up would come out of the pre-money valuation and add a further dilution cost before the new investor's shares are priced. If a pool target has been agreed or is being negotiated, re-running the scenario with that target will show you the real post-round number.\n\n### The one counsel item to track\n\nThere is one item flagged for attorney review: **QSBS eligibility is date-sensitive** (source: TAXADVISER-QSBS-OBBBA). Whether shares qualify under IRC \u00a71202 \u2014 and which version of the rules applies \u2014 turns on the date those shares were acquired. That is a fact your attorney needs from you; it is not something the cap-table math can settle on its own. Bring the share issuance dates to your counsel conversation. This is a question worth asking early, because the answer affects how much of your gain may be excludable from federal tax on an exit.\n\n### Thirteen missing issuance dates\n\nThe date-tracking layer has 13 instrument or grant records with no issuance date on file. These missing dates are not blocking the math in the one scenario modeled, but they matter for two reasons:\n\n1. **QSBS holding-period clock** starts from the date shares (or rights) were acquired. Without that date, no holding-period analysis is possible, and the counsel item above cannot be resolved.\n2. **Other date-sensitive rules** \u2014 including any \u00a7102 or Rule 144 considerations if the company's structure ever involves Israeli-issued equity \u2014 also